<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:zeebe="http://camunda.org/schema/zeebe/1.0" id="Defs_pi_default_loop" targetNamespace="http://graph-agent/bpmn" exporter="graph-agent" exporterVersion="0.1.0">
  <bpmn:process id="pi_default_loop" name="Pi default agent loop" isExecutable="true">
    <bpmn:documentation>Pi's built-in agent loop, drawn.

This is a transcription of runLoop() in @earendil-works/pi-agent-core
(packages/agent/src/agent-loop.ts): an outer follow-up loop wrapped around an
inner turn loop. Pi still performs each turn -- streaming, tool execution,
retries and abort are all Pi's -- but the iteration policy lives here rather
than in a while loop nobody can see. Running the agent under
shouldStopAfterTurn: () =&gt; true reduces Pi's loop to a single step, and this
graph decides whether to take another.

Every branch in runLoop() appears below: the steering drain, the
fail-all-truncated path taken when a response hits the output token limit, the
batch terminate rule, prepareNextTurn, shouldStopAfterTurn, and the follow-up
drain that decides between another turn and stopping.

All of this runs against ONE Pi agent for the whole session. The prompt cache
covers the prefix system prompt -&gt; tools -&gt; messages, so appending to the
transcript keeps every earlier turn cached, while changing the system prompt or
the tool list at a node boundary throws that cache away on every iteration.
Specialise a node through the message it contributes, not by swapping its prompt
or tools. See docs/research/05-pi-loops-and-token-cache.md.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="loop_start" name="Prompt">
      <bpmn:outgoing>to_inject</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="to_inject" sourceRef="loop_start" targetRef="gw_inject_entry" />
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="gw_inject_entry" name="Loop entry">
      <bpmn:documentation>A plain merge of the three ways the inner/outer loop re-enters: a fresh
start, another turn, or a follow-up restarting the outer loop. Explicit
rather than the three-way implicit merge bpmnlint's fake-join rule used to
only warn about (now an error) -- a plain activity with more than one
incoming edge does not join at all in this engine, it just runs again per
arrival, which is exactly the behaviour this gateway keeps.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>to_inject</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>next_turn</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>followup_again</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>into_inject_pending</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="into_inject_pending" sourceRef="gw_inject_entry" targetRef="inject_pending" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="inject_pending" name="Inject pending messages">
      <bpmn:documentation>Drains the steering queue and appends those messages before the next
provider request, matching the top of runLoop's inner while.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:taskDefinition type="agent:steer" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>into_inject_pending</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>to_turn</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="to_turn" sourceRef="inject_pending" targetRef="llm_turn" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="llm_turn" name="LLM turn">
      <bpmn:documentation>Exactly one assistant response. Pi streams it; the token does not move
until the response is complete.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:taskDefinition type="agent:turn" />
        <zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:input source="=prompt" target="prompt" />
          <zeebe:output source="=null" target="prompt" />
          <zeebe:output source="=stop_reason" target="stop_reason" />
          <zeebe:output source="=tool_calls" target="tool_calls" />
          <zeebe:output source="=usage" target="last_usage" />
        </zeebe:ioMapping>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>to_turn</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>to_gw_failed</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="to_gw_failed" sourceRef="llm_turn" targetRef="gw_failed" />
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="gw_failed" name="Errored or aborted?" default="turn_ok">
      <bpmn:incoming>to_gw_failed</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>turn_failed</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>turn_ok</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="turn_failed" name="error / aborted" sourceRef="gw_failed" targetRef="end_error">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">=stop_reason = "error" or stop_reason = "aborted"</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="turn_ok" name="ok" sourceRef="gw_failed" targetRef="gw_tools" />
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="gw_tools" name="Tool calls?" default="no_tools">
      <bpmn:incoming>turn_ok</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>has_tools</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>no_tools</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="has_tools" name="yes" sourceRef="gw_tools" targetRef="gw_truncated">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">=tool_calls != null and count(tool_calls) &gt; 0</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="no_tools" name="no" sourceRef="gw_tools" targetRef="drain_followup" />
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="gw_truncated" name="Response truncated?" default="not_truncated">
      <bpmn:incoming>has_tools</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>truncated</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>not_truncated</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="truncated" name="hit token limit" sourceRef="gw_truncated" targetRef="fail_tool_batch">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">=stop_reason = "length"</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="not_truncated" name="complete" sourceRef="gw_truncated" targetRef="tool_batch" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="fail_tool_batch" name="Fail truncated tool calls">
      <bpmn:documentation>A "length" stop means the arguments of every tool call in the message may
be cut off. None are safe to execute, so each is failed with an error result
and the model is invited to re-issue them.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:taskDefinition type="agent:fail-truncated-tools" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>truncated</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>failed_to_prepare</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="failed_to_prepare" sourceRef="fail_tool_batch" targetRef="gw_prepare_entry" />
    <bpmn:subProcess id="tool_batch" name="Execute tool batch">
      <bpmn:documentation>One instance per tool call in the assistant message. isSequential mirrors
Pi's toolExecution setting; the default there is parallel.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>not_truncated</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>batch_done</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:multiInstanceLoopCharacteristics>
        <bpmn:extensionElements>
          <zeebe:loopCharacteristics inputCollection="=tool_calls" inputElement="tool_call" outputCollection="tool_results" outputElement="=tool_result" />
        </bpmn:extensionElements>
      </bpmn:multiInstanceLoopCharacteristics>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="tool_start" name="Start">
        <bpmn:outgoing>to_tool</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="to_tool" sourceRef="tool_start" targetRef="run_tool" />
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="run_tool" name="Run tool">
        <bpmn:extensionElements>
          <zeebe:taskDefinition type="agent:tool" />
          <zeebe:ioMapping>
            <zeebe:input source="=content.tool_call" target="tool_call" />
            <zeebe:output source="=terminate" target="tool_result" />
          </zeebe:ioMapping>
        </bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bpmn:incoming>to_tool</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>tool_done</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="tool_done" sourceRef="run_tool" targetRef="tool_end" />
      <bpmn:endEvent id="tool_end" name="Done">
        <bpmn:incoming>tool_done</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
    </bpmn:subProcess>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="batch_done" sourceRef="tool_batch" targetRef="collect_batch" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="collect_batch" name="Collect tool results">
      <bpmn:documentation>Appends the batch's tool results to the transcript and reports whether
every one of them asked to terminate -- Pi's rule is all, not any.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:taskDefinition type="agent:collect-tools" />
        <zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:output source="=batch_terminate" target="batch_terminate" />
        </zeebe:ioMapping>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>batch_done</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>collected</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="collected" sourceRef="collect_batch" targetRef="gw_terminate" />
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="gw_terminate" name="Whole batch asked to stop?" default="batch_continues">
      <bpmn:documentation>Pi terminates early only when every finalized tool result in the batch sets
terminate, so this is an all, not an any.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>collected</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>batch_terminates</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>batch_continues</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="batch_terminates" name="all terminate" sourceRef="gw_terminate" targetRef="gw_end_stopped_entry">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">=batch_terminate = true</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="batch_continues" name="continue" sourceRef="gw_terminate" targetRef="gw_prepare_entry" />
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="gw_prepare_entry" name="Turn settled">
      <bpmn:documentation>A plain merge of the two ways a turn's tool batch settles -- the whole
batch ran, or it was failed outright for a truncated response -- onto the
one place that decides whether to loop again, the same reasoning as
gw_inject_entry above.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>batch_continues</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>failed_to_prepare</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>into_prepare_next_turn</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="into_prepare_next_turn" sourceRef="gw_prepare_entry" targetRef="prepare_next_turn" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="prepare_next_turn" name="Prepare next turn">
      <bpmn:documentation>Pi's prepareNextTurn hook: swap context, model or thinking level before the
next provider request. This is also where compaction belongs -- under BPMN
control it is a visible step rather than an invisible transformContext.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:taskDefinition type="agent:prepare-next-turn" />
        <zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:output source="=should_stop" target="should_stop" />
        </zeebe:ioMapping>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>into_prepare_next_turn</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>to_gw_stop</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="to_gw_stop" sourceRef="prepare_next_turn" targetRef="gw_should_stop" />
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="gw_should_stop" name="Stop after this turn?" default="next_turn">
      <bpmn:incoming>to_gw_stop</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>stop_now</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>next_turn</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="stop_now" name="yes" sourceRef="gw_should_stop" targetRef="gw_end_stopped_entry">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">=should_stop = true</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="next_turn" name="another turn" sourceRef="gw_should_stop" targetRef="gw_inject_entry" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="drain_followup" name="Drain follow-up queue">
      <bpmn:documentation>The agent would stop here. runLoop's outer while asks for queued follow-up
messages; if any arrive the inner loop starts again.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:taskDefinition type="agent:follow-up" />
        <zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:output source="=has_followup" target="has_followup" />
        </zeebe:ioMapping>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>no_tools</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>to_gw_followup</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="to_gw_followup" sourceRef="drain_followup" targetRef="gw_followup" />
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="gw_followup" name="Follow-up queued?" default="no_followup">
      <bpmn:incoming>to_gw_followup</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>followup_again</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>no_followup</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="followup_again" name="yes" sourceRef="gw_followup" targetRef="gw_inject_entry">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">=has_followup = true</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="no_followup" name="no" sourceRef="gw_followup" targetRef="end_done" />
    <bpmn:endEvent id="end_done" name="Agent done">
      <bpmn:incoming>no_followup</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="gw_end_stopped_entry" name="Stopping">
      <bpmn:documentation>A plain merge of the two ways this run stops early -- shouldStopAfterTurn
said so, or the whole tool batch asked to terminate -- onto one end event,
the same reasoning as gw_inject_entry above.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>stop_now</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>batch_terminates</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>into_end_stopped</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="into_end_stopped" sourceRef="gw_end_stopped_entry" targetRef="end_stopped" />
    <bpmn:endEvent id="end_stopped" name="Stopped">
      <bpmn:incoming>into_end_stopped</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="end_error" name="Turn failed">
      <bpmn:incoming>turn_failed</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:terminateEventDefinition id="terminate_on_error" />
    </bpmn:endEvent>
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="BPMNDiagram_pi_default_loop">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="BPMNPlane_pi_default_loop" bpmnElement="pi_default_loop">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="loop_start_di" bpmnElement="loop_start">
        <dc:Bounds x="57" y="102" width="36" height="36" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="gw_inject_entry_di" bpmnElement="gw_inject_entry" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="160" y="95" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="100" y="150" width="70" height="20" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="inject_pending_di" bpmnElement="inject_pending">
        <dc:Bounds x="260" y="80" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="llm_turn_di" bpmnElement="llm_turn">
        <dc:Bounds x="400" y="80" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="gw_failed_di" bpmnElement="gw_failed" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="540" y="95" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="515" y="65" width="110" height="20" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="end_error_di" bpmnElement="end_error">
        <dc:Bounds x="547" y="222" width="36" height="36" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="gw_tools_di" bpmnElement="gw_tools" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="650" y="95" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="640" y="65" width="70" height="20" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="gw_truncated_di" bpmnElement="gw_truncated" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="760" y="95" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="730" y="65" width="120" height="20" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="fail_tool_batch_di" bpmnElement="fail_tool_batch">
        <dc:Bounds x="900" y="80" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="gw_prepare_entry_di" bpmnElement="gw_prepare_entry" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="1060" y="95" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="1045" y="65" width="80" height="20" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="prepare_next_turn_di" bpmnElement="prepare_next_turn">
        <dc:Bounds x="1170" y="80" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="gw_should_stop_di" bpmnElement="gw_should_stop" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="1330" y="95" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="1300" y="155" width="110" height="20" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="gw_end_stopped_entry_di" bpmnElement="gw_end_stopped_entry" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="1450" y="95" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="1445" y="65" width="60" height="20" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="end_stopped_di" bpmnElement="end_stopped">
        <dc:Bounds x="1560" y="102" width="36" height="36" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="tool_batch_di" bpmnElement="tool_batch">
        <dc:Bounds x="860" y="200" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="collect_batch_di" bpmnElement="collect_batch">
        <dc:Bounds x="1000" y="200" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="gw_terminate_di" bpmnElement="gw_terminate" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="1140" y="215" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="1090" y="285" width="150" height="20" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="drain_followup_di" bpmnElement="drain_followup">
        <dc:Bounds x="760" y="320" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="gw_followup_di" bpmnElement="gw_followup" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="920" y="335" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="890" y="305" width="110" height="20" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="end_done_di" bpmnElement="end_done">
        <dc:Bounds x="1040" y="342" width="36" height="36" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="to_inject_di" bpmnElement="to_inject">
        <di:waypoint x="93" y="120" />
        <di:waypoint x="160" y="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="into_inject_pending_di" bpmnElement="into_inject_pending">
        <di:waypoint x="210" y="120" />
        <di:waypoint x="260" y="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="to_turn_di" bpmnElement="to_turn">
        <di:waypoint x="360" y="120" />
        <di:waypoint x="400" y="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="to_gw_failed_di" bpmnElement="to_gw_failed">
        <di:waypoint x="500" y="120" />
        <di:waypoint x="540" y="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="turn_failed_di" bpmnElement="turn_failed">
        <di:waypoint x="565" y="145" />
        <di:waypoint x="565" y="222" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="turn_ok_di" bpmnElement="turn_ok">
        <di:waypoint x="590" y="120" />
        <di:waypoint x="650" y="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="has_tools_di" bpmnElement="has_tools">
        <di:waypoint x="700" y="120" />
        <di:waypoint x="760" y="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="no_tools_di" bpmnElement="no_tools">
        <di:waypoint x="675" y="145" />
        <di:waypoint x="675" y="360" />
        <di:waypoint x="760" y="360" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="truncated_di" bpmnElement="truncated">
        <di:waypoint x="810" y="120" />
        <di:waypoint x="900" y="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="not_truncated_di" bpmnElement="not_truncated">
        <di:waypoint x="785" y="145" />
        <di:waypoint x="785" y="240" />
        <di:waypoint x="860" y="240" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="failed_to_prepare_di" bpmnElement="failed_to_prepare">
        <di:waypoint x="1000" y="120" />
        <di:waypoint x="1060" y="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="into_prepare_next_turn_di" bpmnElement="into_prepare_next_turn">
